    "The age idiom בֶּן־שְׁנָתוֹ is split, with old on the construct and a year on the rectum, rather than fused: the ASV spends a word on each side, so rule 30's one-rendering condition is unmet and rule 2 splits it. Its suffix is left unrepresented because no possessive is written."
